{
  "format": "call-of-slop-dress-styles/1",
  "_comment": "Hull dress styles (Source/Constructs/HullDress.cs, docs/sandbox/design/hull-dress.md). A style's palette names its colours; its armour is laid in panels about panel.length m long with panel.gap m between them, each panel one of the patterns, picked from the facet, the panel's index, a salt and its place, so both sides of a ship match. A layer is a slab (d: [from, to] m out, a bevel) or a strip (d: m out); its u (along) and v (across) edges are \"lo\", \"hi\", \"mid\" or {from, frac (of the panel's span), off (added), cap (the most frac x span)}. IT is the Zero Day's (TorpedoFrigateParts.cs uses it: --gen-parts torpedo_frigate_parts --check proves it).",
